.TH tuxxhash n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuxxhash
.PP
xxHash32 (XXH32) in pure Tcl, Tk\-free. A \fBfast, non\-cryptographic\fR hash for content de\-duplication and change detection — not for security. The pure\-Tcl implementation provides the 32\-bit variant and matches the reference xxHash32 bit for bit (verified against the canonical vectors and python\-xxhash).
.PP
Pure Tcl, 8.6+ / 9.x. No dependencies.
.SS Commands
.CS
tuxxhash::xxh32     data ?seed? ?-encoding utf-8|binary?   ;# -> 8 hex chars
tuxxhash::xxh32file path ?seed?                        ;# -> 8 hex chars
.CE
.PP
Like \fBtclutils::tuhash\fR: digests of text are UTF\-8, files hash their bytes. \fBxxh32\fR encodes \fBdata\fR to UTF\-8 before hashing (\fB\-encoding utf\-8\fR, the default), so \fBxxh32 "Größe"\fR is the hash of the 7 bytes \fB47 72 c3 b6 c3 9f 65\fR and equals \fBxxh32file\fR of a UTF\-8 file with that text. \fB\-encoding binary\fR takes \fBdata\fR as raw bytes (each character 0–255) — use it for a binary string, e.g. from \fBbinary format\fR or a channel in \fB\-translation binary\fR. \fBxxh32file\fR always hashes the file's bytes. \fBseed\fR is an optional 32\-bit integer (default 0); it comes before \fB\-encoding\fR.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tuxxhash 0.2
namespace import ::tclutils::tuxxhash::*

xxh32 "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"   ;# -> e85ea4de
xxh32 "" 0                                            ;# -> 02cc5d05
xxh32 "Größe"                                         ;# -> 3a44ca22
xxh32 [binary format c* {0 1 2}] 0 -encoding binary   ;# raw bytes
xxh32file /share/2026/rechnung.pdf                    ;# content fingerprint
.CE
.PP
De\-duplication in a scanner: a cheap \fBxxh32file\fR groups candidates; compare the full bytes (or a strong hash) only within a colliding group.
.SS "xxh32 vs. sha256"
.PP
\fBxxh32\fR is much faster but \fBnot\fR collision\-resistant against an adversary and is only 32 bits wide, so accidental collisions appear in large corpora. Use it to \fIdetect change\fR and to \fIbucket\fR likely duplicates; use \fBsha256\fR (tcllib) when you need a cryptographic guarantee or a wide digest. The 64/128\-bit xxHash variants are not available in pure Tcl — they need the native extension.
.SS Errors
.PP
Error code \fB{TCLUTILS TUXXHASH <REASON>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
REASON	When
\fBSEED\fR	seed is not an integer
\fBOPTION\fR	an argument other than \fB\-encoding\fR, or too many arguments
\fBENCODING\fR	\fB\-encoding\fR is neither \fButf\-8\fR nor \fBbinary\fR
\fBBYTES\fR	\fB\-encoding binary\fR with a character above 255
\fBIO\fR	\fBxxh32file\fR could not open the file
.TE
.SS Testing
.PP
\fBtests/tuxxhash.test\fR checks the output against reference vectors (empty, short, 16\-byte block boundary, long, seeded, binary bytes), UTF\-8 text against the same bytes with \fB\-encoding binary\fR, and the file path. Set \fBTCLUTILS_TM\fR to the module directory and run with \fBtclsh\fR (passes on 8.6 and 9.0).
